            <ArticleTitle>Bony spicules trapped in peri-implant soft tissue: a common unrecognized finding.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1856-1861</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1002/ccr3.1207</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>According to the study, there were unexpected tiny bone spicules being inspected in peri-implant soft tissue. These displaced autogenous bone chips were probably presented when preparing implant sites. The displaced bone spicules seemed not induced significant inflammatory reactions; on contrary, defects of specimens and dissolving bone spicules pictures were demonstrated.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
